WEBVTT

1
00:47:58.018 --> 00:48:00.018
God is so good.

2
00:48:03.018 --> 00:48:11.018
There is a connection between giving and returning and the authority of Christ.

3
00:48:12.018 --> 00:48:19.018
What we have just done, what we have just prayed as a statement, is the power of Jesus, the strength of Jesus.

4
00:48:19.018 --> 00:48:28.018
Did you know that the same resurrection power of Christ, of Jesus Himself, when He rose from the dead, is in you and is in me?

5
00:48:29.018 --> 00:48:32.018
It is that same power that raised Jesus from the dead.

6
00:48:33.018 --> 00:48:39.018
And that same power that has given Jesus the position next to the Father to act as examples for us.

7
00:48:39.018 --> 00:48:45.018
Why does He do that? Why does He sit next to the Father with that same power and with that same strength?

8
00:48:45.018 --> 00:48:50.018
Because He wants us to participate in His power and in His majesty.

9
00:48:50.018 --> 00:49:01.018
That we stand as His church. That we stand not in our own strength, because that own strength is not much, but in the power of Christ.

10
00:49:01.018 --> 00:49:12.018
And if we are willing to have that same mindset of Jesus, of meekness and humility and receiving the authority that God wants to give us.

11
00:49:12.018 --> 00:49:19.018
And when we all rise up in prayer and in worship and in giving, then the world will change.

12
00:49:20.018 --> 00:49:23.018
Do we want this world to change?

13
00:49:24.018 --> 00:49:26.018
Does God want this world to change?

14
00:49:26.018 --> 00:49:29.018
This is truly something that God wants to give us.

15
00:49:29.018 --> 00:49:34.018
And the text that I may take for today, I have taken an NBV translation.

16
00:49:34.018 --> 00:49:41.018
And it says, His divine power, His strength has granted us everything we need for a godly life.

17
00:49:41.018 --> 00:49:48.018
A godly life is not on a cloud with a harp, but it is the real, true life of Jesus Christ.

18
00:49:49.018 --> 00:49:54.018
Who wants to do the will of the Father and not his own will. That is a godly life.

19
00:49:55.018 --> 00:49:59.018
And He has granted us everything in His divine power.

20
00:50:00.018 --> 00:50:03.018
Through the knowledge of Him, thus through the knowledge of Him.

21
00:50:03.018 --> 00:50:08.018
By knowing him who has called us by his majesty and wonderful power.

22
00:50:09.018 --> 00:50:13.018
And what has he done here as a package deal?

23
00:50:14.018 --> 00:50:16.018
His precious and rich promises.

24
00:50:17.018 --> 00:50:19.018
He has promised us so much.

25
00:50:20.018 --> 00:50:22.018
Why? Because we may be his.

26
00:50:23.018 --> 00:50:25.018
Would he not give us everything with Jesus?

27
00:50:27.018 --> 00:50:34.018
And he has done that, for that same power, if we believe in that power, if we trust in that resurrection power.

28
00:50:34.018 --> 00:50:36.018
Then that is a protection for us.

29
00:50:36.018 --> 00:50:44.018
A protection that we would escape the corruption that prevails in this world as a result of desires.

30
00:50:44.018 --> 00:50:48.018
So that we may partake of God's own divine nature.

31
00:50:49.018 --> 00:50:51.018
This is quite something, isn't it?

32
00:50:52.018 --> 00:50:56.018
This is one of the best measures of Jesus when he was here on earth.

33
00:50:56.018 --> 00:50:59.018
And it had to sink in for him too.

34
00:51:00.018 --> 00:51:06.018
And now it is the season for it to sink in with us as his church.

35
00:51:07.018 --> 00:51:14.018
Know that we may also stand on the first Pentecost, the very first Pentecost, filled with the power of Jesus.

36
00:51:14.018 --> 00:51:17.018
And that we may say, Jesus lives.

37
00:51:17.018 --> 00:51:24.018
And he wants to heal you, he wants to restore you, he wants to make you better than you have ever been.

38
00:51:25.018 --> 00:51:33.018
And whenever it has to do with faith and trust, there is struggle, there is always adversity.

39
00:51:33.018 --> 00:51:39.018
But we do not need to be frightened, for Jesus has overcome that world.

40
00:51:39.018 --> 00:51:45.018
And the same as what we do with bringing back our gifts, is giving, is returning.

41
00:51:45.018 --> 00:51:49.018
And giving and returning is actually the vehicle of love.

42
00:51:49.018 --> 00:51:57.018
If we truly love God and if we love His church, if we love the people in this world,

43
00:51:57.018 --> 00:52:02.018
then we show that by returning what God has given us.

44
00:52:02.018 --> 00:52:05.018
Whether it is time, whether it is money, whatever.

45
00:52:05.018 --> 00:52:10.018
But the point is that giving, returning to God, is the most important thing.

46
00:52:10.018 --> 00:52:14.018
We can give nothing of ourselves, we can bring nothing.

47
00:52:14.018 --> 00:52:20.018
But everything we have received from Him, He asks us to return it, so that He can fill us again.

48
00:52:20.018 --> 00:52:23.018
And this way you remain fresh, vibrant, free, and young.

49
00:52:23.018 --> 00:52:30.018
Even if you are 188, you are still young, because His power and His might are so great.

50
00:52:30.018 --> 00:52:35.018
And I want to pray for a blessing here and also for the returning this morning.

51
00:52:35.018 --> 00:52:36.018
Father, I thank You.

52
00:52:36.018 --> 00:52:40.018
You are a covenant God, You are a covenant Father.

53
00:52:40.018 --> 00:52:43.018
Who wants us, as Your children, to rise up.

54
00:52:43.018 --> 00:52:48.018
Not out of our own enthusiasm, but through the revelation of Christ.

55
00:52:48.018 --> 00:52:53.018
Through the spirit of Christ, through the mindset of Christ.

56
00:52:53.018 --> 00:52:56.018
We can do nothing without Jesus.

57
00:52:56.018 --> 00:52:59.018
We can do absolutely nothing without Jesus.

58
00:52:59.018 --> 00:53:02.018
And that is why I pray Christ through us.

59
00:53:02.018 --> 00:53:04.018
Here in the Kempen.

60
00:53:04.018 --> 00:53:06.018
Also through the returning.

61
00:53:06.018 --> 00:53:07.018
Lord, and I thank You for that.

62
00:53:07.018 --> 00:53:11.018
Lord, whether we are worshiping or praying or to worship.

63
00:53:11.018 --> 00:53:14.018
Lord, and bringing back, it all belongs together.

64
00:53:14.018 --> 00:53:20.018
It is all one precious gift that we have received from God.

65
00:53:20.018 --> 00:53:22.018
And I pray this over all of us.

66
00:53:22.018 --> 00:53:26.018
And that we may receive the joy of the Lord in giving.

67
00:53:26.018 --> 00:53:29.018
I bless us all with it, in the name of King Jesus.

68
00:53:36.018 --> 00:53:37.018
Hello, hello.

69
00:53:37.018 --> 00:53:39.018
Am I on?

70
00:53:39.018 --> 00:53:42.018
Here Cindy, can I give this to you?

71
00:53:44.018 --> 00:53:45.018
Hallelujah.

72
00:53:45.018 --> 00:53:47.018
Can we honor the band with a round of applause?

73
00:53:52.018 --> 00:53:53.018
Hallelujah.

74
00:53:55.018 --> 00:53:57.018
Thank you very much, band.

75
00:53:58.018 --> 00:53:59.018
Hallelujah.

76
00:54:01.018 --> 00:54:04.018
Father, in the name of Jesus, I thank You for Your Word.

77
00:54:04.018 --> 00:54:07.018
Lord, I thank You that Your Word has been given to us.

78
00:54:09.018 --> 00:54:15.018
If we had not had Your Word, we would be wandering like a people without a shepherd.

79
00:54:15.018 --> 00:54:20.018
We would be wandering without a compass, we would not know where to go.

80
00:54:20.018 --> 00:54:23.018
And then we would never know Jesus, we would never know the Father.

81
00:54:24.018 --> 00:54:27.018
Then everything would simply be completely blind.

82
00:54:28.018 --> 00:54:29.018
Thank You for Your Word.

83
00:54:30.018 --> 00:54:32.018
Thank You, Lord, that I may bring this today.

84
00:54:32.018 --> 00:54:36.018
And I bless everyone in the room, that our hearts may be open.

85
00:54:36.018 --> 00:54:41.018
So that we may receive the Word for the transformation of our soul. Amen.

86
00:54:47.018 --> 00:54:48.018
Is everyone happy?

87
00:54:50.018 --> 00:54:51.018
Nice.

88
00:54:52.018 --> 00:54:53.018
Me too.

89
00:54:57.018 --> 00:54:58.018
Hallelujah.

90
00:54:59.018 --> 00:55:00.018
Hallelujah.

91
00:55:00.018 --> 00:55:01.018
Where is it warm, huh?

92
00:55:02.018 --> 00:55:03.018
Delightful.

93
00:55:04.018 --> 00:55:05.018
I love it.

94
00:55:08.018 --> 00:55:09.018
Hallelujah.

95
00:55:09.018 --> 00:55:11.018
Okay, so the Bible.

96
00:55:14.018 --> 00:55:21.018
The Bible contains a number of letters in the New Testament.

97
00:55:23.018 --> 00:55:26.018
Bible means library.

98
00:55:27.018 --> 00:55:29.018
From the word biblios.

99
00:55:30.018 --> 00:55:35.018
So the Bible is a library of different books.

100
00:55:35.018 --> 00:55:39.018
So we are talking about the books of the Bible.

101
00:55:41.018 --> 00:55:47.018
But a number of these books are not books, but are actually letters.

102
00:55:47.018 --> 00:55:49.018
And those letters, we have found.

103
00:55:50.018 --> 00:55:53.018
And those letters are of immeasurable value.

104
00:55:53.018 --> 00:55:56.018
They are literally of eternal value.

105
00:55:57.018 --> 00:56:06.018
Despite being written 2000 years ago, they are still for us today like a double-edged sword.

106
00:56:07.018 --> 00:56:13.018
And they serve as guiding and directing for a Christian in our lives.

107
00:56:14.018 --> 00:56:20.018
Well, in the time of Jesus, Jesus had twelve disciples.

108
00:56:20.018 --> 00:56:23.018
A disciple is a learner.

109
00:56:23.018 --> 00:56:25.018
It comes from the word discipline.

110
00:56:25.018 --> 00:56:28.018
So you place yourself under the discipline of a teacher.

111
00:56:28.018 --> 00:56:30.018
Then you are a disciple.

112
00:56:30.018 --> 00:56:33.018
And so Jesus had a number of learners.

113
00:56:33.018 --> 00:56:35.018
He had many learners.

114
00:56:35.018 --> 00:56:43.018
Only he chose twelve of his own learners, whom he wanted to train to ultimately become apostles.

115
00:56:43.018 --> 00:56:48.018
Sometimes I find it nice to pause for a moment at the terminologies of the Bible.

116
00:56:48.018 --> 00:56:51.018
So that we know what we are talking about for a moment.

117
00:56:52.018 --> 00:56:56.018
So, Jesus chooses from all those people who follow him.

118
00:56:57.018 --> 00:57:02.018
He chooses twelve disciples, whom he is training.

119
00:57:02.018 --> 00:57:05.018
As an intern, I would say, in the faith.

120
00:57:05.018 --> 00:57:09.018
Whom he will ultimately send out as apostles.

121
00:57:09.018 --> 00:57:13.018
An apostle is someone who is sent out.

122
00:57:13.018 --> 00:57:16.018
Disciple means you are a learner.

123
00:57:16.018 --> 00:57:19.018
Apostle means you are sent out.

124
00:57:19.018 --> 00:57:20.018
Amen?

125
00:57:20.018 --> 00:57:22.018
Clear so far.

126
00:57:22.018 --> 00:57:30.018
So Jesus has a number of his own disciples who are ultimately sent out to the ends of the earth.

127
00:57:30.018 --> 00:57:32.018
For this was the command of Jesus.

128
00:57:32.018 --> 00:57:36.018
Ultimately, Jesus rose from the grave.

129
00:57:36.018 --> 00:57:42.018
And he says to his disciples in Matthew, at the end of the gospel of Matthew he says.

130
00:57:42.018 --> 00:57:46.018
Now I am done with my work, I will return to the Father.

131
00:57:46.018 --> 00:57:50.018
I send you out, I apostle you out.

132
00:57:50.018 --> 00:57:57.018
To go first to Jerusalem, then to all Judea and Galilee, and then to all the ends of the earth.

133
00:57:57.018 --> 00:58:02.018
The gospel, gospel is euangelion, is a Greek word.

134
00:58:02.018 --> 00:58:08.018
And that means to tell the good news that Jesus Christ is here.

135
00:58:08.018 --> 00:58:16.018
Evangelizing is not so much about trying to invite people to church.

136
00:58:16.018 --> 00:58:21.018
And making sure they get baptized and telling them they need to give their life right now to the Lord.

137
00:58:21.018 --> 00:58:28.018
Evangelizing is actually literally simply the statement, Jesus is here.

138
00:58:28.018 --> 00:58:32.018
Of course we want people to come to church.

139
00:58:32.018 --> 00:58:36.018
Of course we want people to immediately come to repentance on the street.

140
00:58:36.018 --> 00:58:40.018
Of course we want them to be baptized right away at the nearest stream.

141
00:58:40.018 --> 00:58:43.018
Of course we want all those things, we all want them.

142
00:58:43.018 --> 00:58:50.018
But evangelizing is literally just simply the statement, Jesus is here.

143
00:58:50.018 --> 00:58:55.018
And as soon as you say that, the authorities and powers of Satan will tremble.

144
00:58:55.018 --> 00:59:01.018
As soon as you say, Jesus is here, the entire thought process of the powers of Satan changes.

145
00:59:01.018 --> 00:59:03.018
Everyone goes crazy.

146
00:59:03.018 --> 00:59:11.018
So the effect of simply saying, Jesus is here, is already enough to change an entire world.

147
00:59:12.018 --> 00:59:16.018
Disciple, apostle, evangelize.

148
00:59:16.018 --> 00:59:19.018
And from evangelizing come churches.

149
00:59:19.018 --> 00:59:22.018
We have only celebrated 40 years of church.

150
00:59:22.018 --> 00:59:26.018
And that is because a number of apostles, I won't say their names, but there they are.

151
00:59:26.018 --> 00:59:34.018
And a number of apostles went out from their living area, comfortably building careers, starting families.

152
00:59:34.018 --> 00:59:39.018
And eventually they feel sent out to go to a foreign land.

153
00:59:39.018 --> 00:59:41.018
Or to go to a foreign area.

154
00:59:41.018 --> 00:59:44.018
The south of the Netherlands, the north of Belgium.

155
00:59:44.018 --> 00:59:46.018
To evangelize there.

156
00:59:46.018 --> 00:59:52.018
And purely on the statement, Jesus is here, a church arises.

157
00:59:52.018 --> 00:59:55.018
Amazing what God does.

158
00:59:55.018 --> 00:59:58.018
Just on the name of Jesus.

159
00:59:58.018 --> 01:00:01.018
Amazing what God can do.

160
01:00:01.018 --> 01:00:07.018
Just if you say from your soul, just to Him, Lord, you are Lord.

161
01:00:07.018 --> 01:00:09.018
What He can do with your life.

162
01:00:09.018 --> 01:00:11.018
Let alone that He can do things.

163
01:00:11.018 --> 01:00:15.018
If you not only say vertically to Him, Lord, I recognize you as Lord.

164
01:00:15.018 --> 01:00:17.018
Then He can change your life.

165
01:00:17.018 --> 01:00:25.018
But if you start to tell horizontally as well, Jesus is here, Jesus is here, Jesus is here.

166
01:00:25.018 --> 01:00:27.018
Boy, then you can change your whole life.

167
01:00:27.018 --> 01:00:29.018
And everything and everyone around you.

168
01:00:31.018 --> 01:00:35.018
Well, there were all those disciples and those disciples had become apostles.

169
